// ps3t.3.12 regression — consumer-side instantiation of an imported generic
// struct reached through a struct field (direct AND container-WRAPPED), via the
// LIBRARY/METADATA compile path, with the generic instance's method called
// DIRECTLY by the consumer.
//
// The concrete @std `WrappedTables` (core/side_table.av) holds `DenseTable<StmtId,
// int>` three ways:
//   direct : DenseTable<StmtId, int>            (direct field)
//   layers : List<DenseTable<StmtId, int>>      (List-wrapped)
//   opt    : DenseTable<StmtId, int>?            (Optional-wrapped)
// A test shard compiles as a CONSUMER of @std. It obtains the struct from the
// concrete `new_wrapped_tables` constructor (whose body — the only place a
// `DenseTable` is built — stays in the producer, unshipped) and reads the tables
// DIRECTLY: `w.direct.get(id)`, `w.layers[0].get(id)`, `w.opt!.get(id)`. So the
// consumer must monomorphize `DenseTable<StmtId, int>` — collect the inst,
// specialise its struct AND its `.get` method, AND rewrite each field-reached
// reference to the mangled name — with the instance reachable ONLY via
// `WrappedTables`' field types and NO local StructLit / `new_dense_table` call.
//
// This is the first test where a consumer calls a method directly on a generic
// instance reached purely through an imported concrete struct's field (the arena
// tests all go through Arena's own methods, so DenseTable is specialised
// transitively inside Arena's spec, never called directly). Two mono passes must
// both walk field types structurally through wrappers: `collect_inst_from_vtype`
// (collection, ps3t.3.11/#792) AND `rewrite_instance_vtype` (mangling — the
// LIST-wrapped case regressed here: the rewriter recursed into `Optional` but not
// `List`/`Map`/`Tuple`/…, so `store.layers[i]` kept the un-mangled element type
// and `.get` on it failed `undefined method DenseTable.get`; ps3t.3.12).
//
// generic_arena_library_path_test.av covers the field-through-generic-wrapper
// (Arena) path; this covers a consumer calling a field-reached generic
// instance's method directly, direct + through List / Optional wrappers.

use @std.avrac.core.{WrappedTables, new_wrapped_tables, StmtId}

spec "ps3t.3.12: consumer reads a field-reached imported DenseTable directly (direct + wrapped)" {
    then "DIRECT field: written slot + fill round-trip" {
        let w = new_wrapped_tables()
        let d = w.direct
        d.get(StmtId(5)) == 50 && d.get(StmtId(9)) == 0 - 1
    }
    then "LIST-wrapped field: each layer's written slot round-trips through .get" {
        let w = new_wrapped_tables()
        let t0 = w.layers[0]
        let t1 = w.layers[1]
        t0.get(StmtId(2)) == 20 && t1.get(StmtId(3)) == 30
    }
    then "LIST-wrapped field: unwritten slot reads the fill" {
        let w = new_wrapped_tables()
        w.layers[0].get(StmtId(7)) == 0 - 5
    }
    then "OPTIONAL-wrapped field: written slot + fill round-trip through .get" {
        let w = new_wrapped_tables()
        let o = w.opt!
        o.get(StmtId(4)) == 40 && o.get(StmtId(1)) == 0 - 9
    }
    then "the List-wrapped field's own length reads back" {
        let w = new_wrapped_tables()
        w.layers.length == 2
    }
}
